# Copy this file to .env.openrouter beside openrouterAdvisor.py.
# Do not commit .env.openrouter or share its contents.

# Required: an OpenRouter API key (sk-or-...), not an Anthropic or Local server key.
# The router reads it as its upstream credential; do not export it as Claude Code authentication.
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY

# Required: the exact OpenRouter model ID you want to use (provider/model).
# Copy a concrete ID from https://openrouter.ai/models and confirm Messages/tool support.
# There is no default model. Existing key-only files must add this setting.
# Dynamic aliases/presets may return another model ID and fail strict response validation.
OPENROUTER_MODEL=REPLACE_WITH_OPENROUTER_MODEL_ID

# Fixed in code; these are reference values, not additional .env parameters:
# Messages API URL: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/messages
# Request timeout: 30 seconds per attempt.
# Retry policy: initial attempt + 3 retries, with 1 second between attempts.
# Recovery cooldown: 30 seconds before a later request checks recovery.
# Failure fallback: saved Claude Plan Sonnet; OpenRouter provider fallback is disabled.
# Opus/Haiku/Fable and unsupported native features retain the Plan route.
# Experimental CLI betas are disabled for this routing mode (CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_BETAS,
# CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_ADVISOR_TOOL): external Messages providers reject their inline request shape.

# Launch: .\startClaudeOpenRouter.ps1 -Provider OpenRouter
# Existing Claude Plan login is required for this routing mode.
# Optional separate mode: .\startClaudeOpenRouter.ps1 -Provider OpenRouter -OpenRouterCompat
# Uses the same two required settings above; no additional .env parameter is needed.
# Compat routes all Claude model roles to OPENROUTER_MODEL, without Plan login/fallback.
# Client plugins/skills/MCP/hooks/subagents/effort remain enabled with default permissions.
# Compat uses buffered responses, one 120-second attempt and a 30-second cooldown.
# Interactive startup checks inference once (15 seconds); failure logs a warning and continues.
# -LocalMode and -LocalCompat are Local-provider options, not OpenRouter options.
# For a Local server, use .env.local-llm.example instead; this file is not read in Local mode.
